	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "9 mm potentiometer standing on the board, shaft up, Bourns PTV09A-4 (rear mount, bushingless; the -1, -5 and -6 share the holes): three pins 2.5 mm apart in 1.0 mm holes, two mounting legs 1.8 mm wide in 2.2 mm holes 8.8 mm apart and 7.0 mm behind the pins. Drawn from the maker's recommended PCB layout (horizontal/rear mount), https://www.bourns.com/docs/Product-Datasheets/ptv09.pdf. The three pins sit where the Alpha RD901F-40's do (KiCad's Potentiometer_Alpha_RD901F-40-00D_Single_Vertical), pin 1 the counter-clockwise end, so a board drawn for the Alpha takes this part with only its two leg holes changed.")
